{
  "_meta": {
    "table": "visual_config",
    "source": "docs/VISUAL_STYLE.md, sections 2.4, 3 and 16, translated to Godot 4",
    "notes": [
      "The one place for every visual tunable: colours, widths, thresholds, tier switches and accessibility. Scripts read it through the Visual autoload; none of these numbers is repeated in code.",
      "Every value is a starting point to tune by eye. Press F4 in a debug build to edit any of them live; Save writes your changes to user://visual_overrides.json, which is laid over this file at start-up.",
      "Colours are #RRGGBB strings. A value is addressed by its dotted path, for example palette.cave.fog.",
      "renderer.tonemap: linear keeps flat colours exactly as authored and is the default. agx needs Godot 4.4 or newer. Godot has no Khronos Neutral tone mapper; aces is deliberately not offered as a default because it shifts hand-picked hues.",
      "renderer.antialiasing: off, fxaa, msaa2x or msaa4x. The project runs on Godot's Compatibility renderer, which has no fxaa; there fxaa means msaa2x.",
      "Read since Pass 0: renderer, post, fog, palette.cave.fog; accessibility is stored. Read since Pass 1: lights, toon, outline, blob_shadow, seal, water, props and the palette groups cave, slime, veldora, seal, herb and ore. The ui and elements palettes, slime.face_enabled, quality and tiers are read by later passes.",
      "lights.fill_* is the ambient light of the scene. Toon surfaces ignore it (their shade tint does that job), so it only touches a model that has not been given the toon material.",
      "lights.shadow_min_part_size: a creature part thinner than this (metres) casts no shadow, nor do eyes and other accents.",
      "lights.shadow_splits is 1, 2 or 4 (more splits keep near shadows sharp); lights.shadow_filter is 0 (hard) to 5 (softest), re-thresholded to a crisp edge by shadow_edge_low and shadow_edge_high.",
      "lights.key_pitch and key_yaw aim the one key light, in degrees: pitch -90 is straight down. toon.character_light_* is the direction characters are lit from, relative to the camera (x right, y up, z toward the viewer).",
      "outline widths are pixels at a screen height of outline.reference_height. An asset's own width is outline_px in data/asset_manifest.json; outline.scale multiplies them all.",
      "shade tints are multiplied onto a surface's colour in its shaded band. An asset that names its own shade colour (the palette pairs) uses that instead."
    ]
  },
